WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Canadian investors holding US equities in TFSAs should review allocations as the S&amp;P 500 reaches new all-time highs. This is Modern Investing Techniques episode 192. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:41.900
work. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,841, up 0.9%. The NASDAQ composite reached 27,714, also

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:53.040
up 0.9%. The TSX composite finished at 35,698, up 0.5%. The US economy has now expanded

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:59.280
for 78 straight months without a recession. The sixth longest streak since 1854 according

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.700
according to the N-B-E-R. About 14 days ago, we picked G-O-O-G-L on an AI-powered

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:12.240
demand theme, and it closed down 4.17 percent, showing even strong sector stories can face

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:20.080
rotation pressure. The NASDAQ sits at a year-to-date gain of 19.27 percent. Rate-sensitive sectors

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.440
remain in focus ahead of the next Bank of Canada and Federal Reserve decisions, with options

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:32.360
flow showing heavy call buying on the SNPY at the 790 strike. The long economic expansion

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:37.320
creates a stable backdrop for sector rotation strategies that shift exposure toward areas

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:43.160
showing relative strength rather than broad index holding. Today's data shows the current

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:49.020
cycle already exceeds the historical average of 49 months, giving investors time to identify

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:55.020
which sectors absorb inflows while others lag. Implementation starts with a screener that ranks

00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:01.340
TSX and NASDAQ sectors by relative performance over the past 20 sessions, then cross-checks

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:04.500
volume against the 20-day average before committing capital.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:10.440
This approach worked well in 2023 when tech rotated ahead of the broader market on AI

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.960
spending, delivering outperformance for disciplined followers.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:20.040
Risks include sudden policy shifts or geopolitical events that can override the rotation signal,

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.740
as seen when defense spending announcements briefly lifted industrials without sustained

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:25.520
follow-through.

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:32.420
Canadian investors can execute this inside a TFSA by using low-cost sector ETFs on quest

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.440
trade or wealth simple and rebalancing only when the volume filter confirms the move.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:43.080
The key is requiring volume above the 20-day average before entering any name already

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:45.840
in a rotation, per the active rule set.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.960
Imagine you bought an ETF tracking Canadian banks last spring at a higher price, and it

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:55.900
now sits 10% below your cost base inside your TFSA.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:02.200
The superficial loss rule means you cannot simply sell and repurchase the identical ETF within

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.940
30 days without losing the ability to claim the capital loss for tax purposes.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:14.080
Instead, you sell the original holding, immediately by a similar but not identical ETF, such as

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.460
one focused on broad Canadian equities, and hold that substitute for the full 30-day window

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.260
before switching back if desired.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.860
Professionals always check the T-508 slip issued by their broker in February to confirm

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.440
the adjusted cost base and reported proceeds match their records.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:37.100
The capital gains inclusion rate change means losses now offset a higher portion of gains,

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.420
making the harvest more valuable for accounts that realize gains elsewhere.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:47.120
The concrete misconception to avoid is treating any sale within 30 days as harmless.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:53.300
The fix is mapping the exact 30-day window on your calendar, the moment you execute the harvest.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:01.180
We simulated buying X and DU on a catalyst play tied to the multi-year manufacturing partnership with global foundries.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.640
The entry uses shares with a five-session hold starting at the next open.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:10.960
The invalidation level sits at any failure of the announcement to produce volume above the

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.960
20-day average within two sessions.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:20.260
Risk is capped at 8% below entry, while the target range runs from plus 3% to plus 7%.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:25.540
This setup demonstrates how to evaluate a genuine fundamental catalyst against the volume

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:28.900
filter required by our current rules before committing capital.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:34.700
Listeners learn to require both the news event and confirming volume rather than entering

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:44.220
on announcement alone. We simulated buying iag.to at the Tuesday open of $207.52. The position

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:55.000
exited at the Monday close of $203.93. The trade lost 1.73% or $17.30 on the $1,000 position.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:00.960
The thesis around sustained inflows into segregated funds did not produce the expected price

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.780
follow-through during the holding window. The volume filter was not met on the entry day,

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:11.420
allowing rotation pressure to dominate. The rules-based record that began on August 18,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:21.480
2026 now stands at 71 total trades with a 52% win rate. Cumulative simulated profit reaches $303.95.

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:29.720
The matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ composite sits at negative 15.41% across 20 rules-based

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:35.640
trades. The record continues to rebuild after the recent drawdown by applying tighter volume and

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:42.220
sector filters on each new entry. The unusual Wales Options Flow Scanner surfaces large options

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:49.420
trades in real-time, including the 60,000 S&amp;PY 790 calls that opened at the start of trading today.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:56.640
Canadian investors can use the free tier to monitor unusual activity on US names held in their TFSAs

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.100
and cross-reference with volume data before adding exposure.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:05.740
The edge comes from seeing institutional positioning early rather than reacting to price moves

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:06.680
after the fact.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:13.000
The wealth-simple-trade sector screener lets users rank TSX and US listings by relative

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:18.780
sector performance and 20-day volume, directly supporting the rotation approach discussed earlier.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.340
Investors set alerts for names crossing above average volume while in a leading sector,

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:28.740
then review the position inside their TFSA or RRSP.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:31.540
This replaces manual spreadsheet tracking

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.440
and reduces the chance of missing confirmation signals.

